<!--
  A fixture of the EU consolidated list of financial sanctions (file xmlFullSanctionsList_1_1, XSD
  1.1), with fictional names and hosts under .example, in the shape of the real file.

  Checked against the real XML 1.1 and its XSD on 2026-10-31 (generated 2026-10-23: 6,269 entries,
  1,779 of them enterprises): the connector read every enterprise with no error, and every path
  below is declared in the XSD and present in the file, except sanctionEntity@delistingDate, which
  no entry carries. An entry that leaves the list leaves the file, and the mirror marks it delisted
  by its absence. Entry 1104 keeps a delistingDate all the same, as the XSD allows.

  The paths the connector reads:
    /export@generationDate                        the list's version (the root also has globalFileId)
    /export/sanctionEntity@logicalId, @euReferenceNumber, @designationDate, @delistingDate,
      @unitedNationId                             on every entry, filled on 23 of the enterprises
    /export/sanctionEntity/subjectType@classificationCode      P for a person, E for an enterprise
    /export/sanctionEntity/nameAlias@wholeName, @firstName, @middleName, @lastName, @nameLanguage
    /export/sanctionEntity/regulation@programme
    /export/sanctionEntity/address/contactInfo@key, @value     only the key WEB
    /export/sanctionEntity/identification@number, @identificationTypeCode

  The shape of the real file, which the fixture keeps:
    - The root declares the namespace http://eu.europa.ec/fpi/fsd/export. An entry lists remark
      (not always), regulation, subjectType, nameAlias (one or more), address and identification,
      in that order.
    - Every nameAlias carries strong="true", so none is the main one. Its nameLanguage is a
      language code or empty (empty on 1,617 of the 14,327 aliases of enterprises), and 863 of the
      1,779 enterprises list an alias in another language than English first: entry 1101 does.
    - A name is in wholeName, and firstName, middleName and lastName are empty. The XSD makes
      wholeName optional, and the file always has it: entry 1105 has none, to check the parts.
    - Contact details are contactInfo children of an address, with the key EMAIL, PHONE, FAX or
      WEB. A WEB value is a site with or without its scheme (118 of the 556 values of enterprises
      are written without one), may hold several sites separated by white space, a comma or a
      semicolon (64 do), and once holds an e-mail address typed into the field: entry 1101 has
      both. Pages on platforms where many have pages (t.me, vk.com) are common.
    - unitedNationId is on every entry and mostly empty: entry 1101 carries a UN reference number.
    - Entry 1102 lists its regulation twice, which the XSD does not allow (one regulation per
      entry) and the file never does. The connector tolerates it and lists the programme once.
  Left out, as the connector reads none of it: the regulationSummary and publicationUrl elements;
  the function, gender and title of an alias; most attributes of an address and of an
  identification; and the citizenship and birthdate elements of a person.
-->
